NAME
    vash - VNU shell

SYNOPSIS
    vash

DESCRIPTION
    The interactive login shell. Prints a prompt of the form
    user@name:cwd$, where name comes from /etc/hostname, and reads
    commands line by line. Words are
    split on whitespace; there is no quoting or piping yet.

    Redirection is supported with > file, >> file (append) and
    < file; the operators may be attached or space-separated.

    On a cold boot vash runs the login sequence (VNU login: /
    Password:) against /etc/passwd. After an external command
    the kernel respawns it and it silently re-adopts the session
    it saved to /tmp/.session, so a 'logout' (exit) returns to
    the login prompt.

    Editor keys: Up/Down history, Ctrl+C cancels a line, Shift
    is used to type symbol characters.

    Also installed as /bin/sh, /sbin/init and as the GUI's
    'term' app - see man sh, man init, man term.

OPTIONS
    none.
